rtant technical  details  out of the way let's get into some  numbers lots  of numbers metro exodus is one of the  most demanding games out there and it  includes full ray tracing  options as well as dlss and the built-in  benchmark is a good stress test  at 4k with every setting maxed average  frame rate output came out to 51.6  fps for the rtx 3080. this comes out to  a 24.6  increase over the 2080 ti and a 63.8  percent improvement  over the 2080. at 1440p average frame  rate came out to 67.2 fps for the 3080  a 20.4 percent increase and 54.8 percent  increase over the 2080 ti and 2080  respectively  control is visually enticing demanding  and full of graphics options  we turned every ray tracing option on  maxed out settings  and used the lss since control doesn't  have a built-in benchmark we made our  own by running through an early section  of the old house that was easily  repeatable and used fraps to record the  average  fps at 4k average frame rate came out to  64 fps  on the rtx 3080. this makes for a 35  jump from the 2080 ti and a whopping  103.2 percent increase over the 2080.  at 1440p average frame rate came out to  104.6  fps for the 3080 which marks a 27.1  percent  and 59.7 percent increase over the  respective 2080 ti  and 2080 cards shadow of the tomb raider  remains a graphical showcase with lush  detailed environments  and features ray tracing and dlss  running at 4k with everything maxed  the rtx 3080 got a 70 fps average  these are 22.8 percent and 62.8 percent  increases over the 2080 ti and 2080  respectively  running at 1440p the 3080 hit an average  of 100 fps  which comes out to 16.3 percent and 49.5  increases over the respective cards  wolfenstein youngblood isn't the most  graphically demanding game  but we can measure performance in the id  tech 6 engine  with ray tracing and dlss we use the  riverside benchmark run  with everything at max settings at 4k we  got an average frame  rate of 117 fps for the 3080.  this result makes for a jump of 31.5  percent  and 69.6 against the 2080 ti  and 2080. at 1440p average frame rate  came out to 171 fps  on the 3080 meaning smaller gains of  18.8 percent  and 45 over the 2080 ti and 2080.  final fantasy 15 is a visual powerhouse  with a robust benchmark test  while it doesn't have ray tracing it has  other nvidia features including dlss  note that this benchmark does not give  average fps  rather produces a total score at 4k with  max settings  the rtx 3080 scored 7281  this comes out to 20.1 percent and 35.2  performance increases against the 2080  ti  and 2080. for 1440p the final fantasy 15  bench does not allow dlss  so here we just use the high quality  settings preset  and here the rtx 3080 scored 11  381 which comes out to 14.2 percent  and 36.4 performance increases  well what can i say shadowbringers is  the best expansion for an  all-time favorite game in final fantasy  14.  you know i had to do it to him there's  also a free benchmark tool out there  this one also produces a score rather  than average fps  at 4k max the rtx 3080 scored  14 138 indicating performance jumps of  22.1 percent  and 58 against the 2080 ti  and 2080. at 1440p we have the 3080  scored at 17626  which shows minimal gains over its 2080  counterparts  here we see a lower spec game like final  fantasy 14  reach its upper limit of gpu reliance  and become more cpu bound with minor  performance increases  between cards red dead redemption 2 is  certainly graphically demanding with a  slew of options to help tweak your  performance  we turned everything up to max but just  went with taa for anti-aliasing  at 4k average frame rate came out to  43.1 fps  for the 3080 which marks increases of  16.2 percent  and 52.3 percent over the 2080 ti  and 2080. at 1440p average frame rate  came out to 62.9 fps  with the 3080 and these numbers indicate  increases of 21  and 61.3 percent over the respective  2080 cards  assassin's creed odyssey remains a  visually stunning and demanding game  though it tends to be cpu heavy it's  still important to see how high-end  video cards fare here  at 4k the 3080 got an average of 62 fps  which comes out to respective gains of  19.2 percent  and 51.2 percent in performance using  1440p  the 3080 hidden average of 78 fps  which is a decent improvement but not  significant compared to other tests  like final fantasy 14 assassin's creed  odyssey at 1440p  starts a show where the workload leans  heavier into the cpu  limiting the effectiveness of a beefy  gpu  horizon zero dawn just got ported to pc  with mixed results  it's had some improvements since its  launch and has a decent benchmark tool  to stress our video cards though  at 4k average fps counts came out to 75  fps  for the 3080 and these results show 31.6  percent  and 66.7 increases from the two other  cards  using 1440p average frame rate was 109  fps with the 3080  coming out to 13.5 percent and 39.7  jumps for the 3080 over the respective  cards  and finally forza horizon 4 a beautiful  open world racing game with a wildly  detailed benchmark tool  at 4k and everything maxed including  msaa the 3080 hit an average of 96  fps which is a jump of 28  and 50.8 over the 2080 ti  and 2080. going to 1440p  average framerate came out to 129 fps  for the 3080  which comes out to 15.2 percent and 35.8  against the respective cards so after  all those numbers  benchmarks and graphic settings the  takeaway is this  the rtx 3080 is a powerful card with big  generational jumps  especially when considering its 700 msrp  the rtx 3080 shows decent gains over the  rtx  2080 ti which is a card that came out  the gate  much more expensive and the 3080 shows  significant improvements over the base  rtx 2080.  nvidia's claim of up to twice as fast as  the 2080 is  a bit of a stretch although this was  true and a big game like control  nvidia tempered expectations a little  bit by saying we'd see closer to 60  percent gains  and that much is true based on our  results and that improvement is nothing  to scoff at  however whether or not you should buy an  rtx 3080 depends on how you want to run  your games  it's your best option for 4k capable of  60fps  at max settings with little to no  compromises  however the improvements tend to taper  off at 1440p  regardless it's a better value than the  2080 ti  and 2080 at this point even if the gains  aren't as apparent at 1440p  but if you don't really care about 4k or  you aren't trying to push your high  refresh rate 1440p monitor to its limits  i consider the rtx 3080 overkill  for now if those aspects aren't your jam  you probably want to keep an  eye on the upcoming rtx 3070. either way  if you're still on a gtx 10 series card  this might be a good generation to hop  on with great features like dlss for  simultaneous image quality  and performance improvements and ray  tracing which is increasingly relevant  in games  not to mention the boost in raw  performance so yes while the rtx 3080 is  an incredible card  just make sure it's something that  you're actually getting the most out of  for a little more in-depth analysis be  sure to check out my full written review  on gamespot.com thanks for watching  [Music]  wow
 

